//? Title: Move-to-front recoding
//? Subtitle: Actual alphabet ranks, reversible moves and the original BWT example
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Recode a byte stream so that recently seen bytes receive small integer ranks
while preserving every original byte exactly. Move-to-front maintains an
evolving alphabet that encoder and decoder can reproduce together. We inspect
actual moves on four bytes, retain the original repetitive-text/BWT example, and
measure real rank distributions and work without claiming that integer ranks
alone compress the data.
)

\toc

> The shared permutation is the invariant

Start with the unsigned-byte alphabet0..255. For each byte, encode its current
zero-based position, move preceding entries one place right and put the selected
byte at the front. The decoder looks up the received position in its identical
current permutation and performs the same move. Initially the permutations
agree; if they agree before one byte, the rank selects the same byte and both
updates agree afterward. Induction proves exact reversibility, including NUL and
bytes128..255.

A repeated byte after its first occurrence has rank zero, since it is already at
the front. A byte revisited after other distinct bytes has rank equal to the
number of distinct bytes used since its previous occurrence. First occurrences
instead depend on the initial unsigned-byte order. These are recency statements,
not an entropy-coding algorithm. The returned vector stores ints; its memory
representation can be larger than the original bytes.

> Four actual moves: ABBA

Starting from the full256-byte alphabet, ABBA produces ranks65,66,0,1. The two B
bytes demonstrate the rank-zero rule. The final A is behind only B, so its rank
is one. Every node below reads the actual selected byte, rank and previous front
from the producer, and the table records actual equality tests and shifts.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/mtf_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/move_to_front.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::mtf_encode_trace("ABBA");
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    std::print("| position | byte as integer | actual rank | previous front byte | actual comparisons | " "actual shifts |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &s : t.steps) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.index,
                   unsigned(s.byte), s.rank, unsigned(s.front_before),
                   s.comparisons, s.shifts);
        auto id = std::to_string(s.index);
        d.node(id, {6.0 * s.index, 0},
               std::format("Actual byte {}\nrank {} / new front {}",
                           char(s.byte), s.rank, char(s.byte)));
        if (s.index)
            d.edge(std::to_string(s.index - 1), id);
    }
    std::print("\nNative inverse: {}.\n",
               dm::algorithms::mtf_decode(t.result.indices));
    d.save_svg("build/mtf_tiny.svg");
}
```
