| position | byte as integer | actual rank | previous front byte | actual comparisons | actual shifts |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 0 | 65 | 65 | 0 | 66 | 65 |
| 1 | 66 | 66 | 65 | 67 | 66 |
| 2 | 66 | 0 | 66 | 1 | 0 |
| 3 | 65 | 1 | 66 | 2 | 1 |

Native inverse: ABBA.
\image(figures/mtf_tiny.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual ranks and moves for the full-byte-alphabet ABBA example.)
\alttext(The observed ranks65,66,0,1 are inverted to ABBA by the native decoder.)

> Retain the original repetitive text after BWT

The original text repeats “the quick brown fox” four times with intervening
spaces. The native cyclic Burrows–Wheeler transform retains its primary row and
appends no sentinel. MTF then recodes its transformed bytes. The full pipeline
inverse first decodes the MTF ranks and then applies the BWT inverse with that
original primary row; discarding that row would lose required BWT information.

The original three rank buckets are retained, but median and mean are now
actually computed instead of printing an assumed median. Empirical marginal
entropy describes this rank distribution; it is not a measured compressed file
size. This example illustrates the BWT/MTF stages rather than claiming to
implement a complete bzip2 stream.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/mtf_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/move_to_front.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/burrows_wheeler.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto text = dm::algorithms::mtf_demo_text();
    auto bw = dm::algorithms::bwt_transform(text);
    auto encoded = dm::algorithms::mtf_encode_analyze(bw.transformed);
    auto summary = dm::algorithms::mtf_index_summary(encoded.indices);
    auto decoded = dm::algorithms::mtf_decode(encoded.indices);
    bool restored = dm::algorithms::bwt_inverse({decoded, bw.index}) == text;
    std::print("| bytes | BWT primary row | full round trip | median rank | mean rank | empirical marginal " "entropy bits/rank |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | " "{} |\n",
               text.size(), bw.index, restored, summary.median, summary.mean,
               summary.entropy_bits);
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(summary.zeros),
                                      double(summary.one_to_three),
                                      double(summary.four_or_more)},
                                     {"0", "1..3", "4..255"},
                                     "actual rank counts");
    p.title("Original repetitive text: MTF ranks after cyclic BWT").x_label(
        "rank bucket").y_label("observed bytes").save_svg(
        "build/mtf_original.svg");
}
```
